    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d730">

                <pb facs="0839" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/10352a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bundy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-03T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s May 31, 3 p.m. Department is advised by French Embassy here that
                    French wireless station in Liberia cannot be put in condition for service for
                    some time and that meanwhile it is necessary to utilize the German wireless
                    station. Cable if Liberian Government is offering objection to use of German
                    station.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
